# Monthly spend cap per bot. Compares each bot's month-to-date cost (OpenMausBot's usage
# ledger, through the framework's observability export) with `botMonthlyUsd` in
# project/observability.json. It ALERTS: the run fails the first time a bot goes over
# its cap in a month, so it shows in Dagu and in the panel's Observability alerts.
# It never pauses a bot: OpenMausBot 0.1.141 has no per-bot limit to switch on.
description: Alert when a bot goes over its monthly spend cap (alert only, never pauses)
type: graph
{% if spend_schedule %}schedule: "{{ spend_schedule }}"
{% endif %}max_active_runs: 1
working_dir: ${FYSO_ROOT}
steps:
  - id: check
    run: node extensions/ops-assistant/digest.cjs spend
    output: RESULT
